{#
  Courrier sortant › Tableau de bord (roadmap IT-03).

  **Three lines, then everything else.** That separation is the whole
  screen. A volunteer opening this page is asking one question — « est-ce
  que les e-mails partent ? » — and a page that lists a dozen equally
  weighted settings answers it for nobody. The advanced options are listed
  underneath with their state and are never collapsed behind a toggle:
  hiding them makes them unfindable, and giving them the same weight as
  the three drowns the message.

  And the page says what it cannot see. Three green lines with no such
  sentence let somebody conclude that everything is fine while a provider
  is quietly filing the lot as spam.
#}
{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Courrier sortant — {{ site_name }}{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
{% include 'partials/page_header.html.twig' with {
    title: 'Courrier sortant',
    subtitle: "Trois choses suffisent pour que les messages du site arrivent. Tout le reste est facultatif.",
} only %}

{% include 'config/outbound_mail/_nav.html.twig' %}

{% set icons = {
    'ok': 'bi-check-circle-fill text-success',
    'warning': 'bi-exclamation-triangle-fill text-warning',
    'missing': 'bi-x-circle-fill text-danger',
    'unknown': 'bi-question-circle-fill text-body-secondary',
} %}

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h5">L'essentiel</h2>
        <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
            {% for line in essentials %}
                <li class="d-flex gap-3 align-items-start {{ loop.last ? '' : 'mb-3' }}">
                    <i class="bi {{ icons[line.state] }} fs-5" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                    <div class="flex-grow-1">
                        <div class="fw-semibold">{{ line.label }}</div>
                        <div class="small text-body-secondary">{{ line.detail }}</div>
                    </div>
                    <a href="{{ line.action_url }}" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary flex-shrink-0">
                        {{ line.action_label }}
                    </a>
                </li>
            {% endfor %}
        </ul>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="alert alert-secondary" role="note">
    Un message classé en indésirables n'apparaît nulle part ici : il a été accepté.
    Cet écran dit si les messages <em>partent</em> et si ce qui revient <em>arrive</em> — pas ce qu'un
    destinataire en fait ensuite.
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-body">
        <h2 class="h5">Options avancées</h2>
        <p class="text-body-secondary small">
            Aucune n'est nécessaire pour que les messages partent. Elles sont listées avec leur état plutôt que
            masquées : une option qu'on ne trouve pas est une option qui n'existe pas.
        </p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
            <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-0">
                <tbody>
                    {% for option in advanced %}
                        <tr>
                            <th scope="row" class="fw-normal">
                                <a href="{{ option.url }}">{{ option.label }}</a>
                                <div class="small text-body-secondary">{{ option.detail }}</div>
                            </th>
                            <td class="small text-body-secondary">{{ option.state_label }}</td>
                        </tr>
                    {% endfor %}
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
